WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.434
-Adam Driver,
welcome back to the show, bud.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.434
-Thank you.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.534
-You look good, pal.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:06.300
-I want to ask you
some questions here,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.767
because I was doing
some reading up about you.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.234
And I know that you studied --

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:12.367
you went to theatre school here
in New York, at Juilliard.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:13.534
-Yeah.
-In New York City.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.334
And I heard that sometimes
you would run

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:18.100
from your apartment to --
to class.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.501
-I did, yeah, yeah.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:21.968
-And you lived in --
-I live in Queens, yeah.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.567
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:27.067
-And Juilliard's on the Midtown,
I would say on the West Side.

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.234
I couldn't --
Yeah, I did do that, yeah.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:32.234
-So, all the time, or --
-I did it for, like,

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.234
during the summer, I would say.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.267
There was
the 59th Street Bridge,

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.934
and I think I'd just
come out of the military.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.167
So, I was trying to make
everything that I was doing as

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.100
difficult as what it was like
being in the military.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.300
And acting school didn't seem
like it fit the criteria,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.367
so I tried to make it
more impossible

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:50.968
than what it needed to be.
-Wow!

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.300
-Yeah, I don't know
why I did that.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.267
-Yeah. I think it's cool
that you did that.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.534
But then once you got to school,
what happened?

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.167
-Well, then we had movement
class with a guy named Daryl,

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.467
where we would --
it's like an exercise class.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:02.934
So, I would start that
as a warm-up,

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.434
and then we'd do
the exercise class.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.000
-And you were like,
"Dude, I just ran for --"

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.634
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Yeah, yeah.
-Wow.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.334
And would you be exhausted?
-Yeah, and sweaty.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.234
Yeah.

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:12.367
[ Laughter ]
-And hungry.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:13.400
-And hungry, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.133
-Mad.
-Really hungry.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.133
-And -- start acting school.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.467
[ Laughter ]
-That's wild though.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:21.667
Once you started to be an actor,

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.601
do you remember
your first big paycheck

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:24.834
and what you spent it on?

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:30.234
-My first -- Well, my first big
paycheck was for "Law &amp; Order."

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:32.033
That was the first thing
I got -- in my mind.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:33.200
-That's very --
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.200
-That's very New York.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.234
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.000
Actually, what I bought
is a pair of Jordans,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.734
because when I was --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.334
I can't --
like we didn't have --

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:46.033
we didn't have any money for --
I mean, we had money for shoes.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.901
But it was never -- you know, we
couldn't afford to buy Jordans.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.901
So, when I actually got paid
to be an actor,

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:52.934
I don't know why, again --
well, I do know why,

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:55.567
because I wanted a pair of
Jordans that I could never have.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.901
-Yeah, but I would think it
would go to something else.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.200
I mean, but that's like --
but that's --

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.934
-No, 'cause I had rent and all
that other [bleep].

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:02.067
So -- stuff.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.701
[ Laughter ]
So, by the time it was over,

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.200
all I had was money --

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.167
Well, I had more money than that
to save.

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:08.901
But the Jordans were the first
thing that I wanted.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.300
-And what kind of Jordans
were they?

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.734
Were they special?
-No, no, no.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:14.968
I think I went and grabbed the
first Jordans that I could find.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.968
I couldn't tell you,
even now, what they are.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:18.300
Like, they're not --
I know they're not Jordan 1s.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.234
They're not the Jordan 4s.
They're not the Jordan 5s.

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.734
I bought them,
and they're on a shelf,

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:24.567
and I don't look at them,
you know.

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:26.667
[ Laughter ]
-Did you ever wear them?

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.267
-No, I don't wear them. No.
-No.

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:29.801
Never wore them?
-No, not all.

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.167
-Because you were saving them
for a special occasion?

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.334
-Not even saving them.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.734
I just wanted them,
and I have them.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.067
They have dust on them.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:36.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.067
-Did you want them
to collect them?

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.968
-No. No.
No, I didn't want to --

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.467
I don't want to wear them,

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:43.767
'cause I don't want to
mess them up.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.968
But I have to dust them off,
because they're dusty.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.133
-Yeah, and this is

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.934
after acting school.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.234
-So, you're not really running
anymore.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.767
-[ Chuckles ] No.
-You don't really need sneakers.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:52.868
-No, and you shouldn't run
in Jordans.

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:54.200
-You shouldn't run in Jordans
anyway.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.100
They're basketball sneakers.
But, yeah, interesting.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.234
Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.767
-I want to --
Next time, if you're here,

00:02:58.767 --> 00:02:59.968
could you --
could you bring them?

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.534
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I'd love to see them.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.934
-I won't touch the dust.
-Yeah.

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:06.067
Let's see what they are,
and then we'll discover,

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.734
like, what kind and --
what kind Adam Driver bought.

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.100
Your first Jordans.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.868
-Let's talk about your movie,
"65."

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.267
Congrats on this.

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:15.133
This is a --
If I can explain it right,

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:17.968
you're a pilot who kind
of is stranded on the Earth,

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:20.667
65 million years ago.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.033
-It's not a time travel movie.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.901
You -- Actually, this is just
set 65 million years ago.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:27.267
-Right, right. Yeah.
There's no time travel.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.267
It's a parallel universe
that they're saying

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:30.934
that existed
65 million years ago,

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.734
and they find that they've crash
landed on prehistoric Earth.

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:36.300
-Wow. What drew you to that?

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.434
Just dinosaurs?
-It was my --

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:39.400
Yeah, basically.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.100
My son likes dinosaurs.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.534
-So, I'm like, "I'm in."

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:44.400
Well, it's dinosaurs
and laser guns,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.734
and I'm like, "Yeah, sure."
-Yeah.

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.801
-And it was actually --
it was actually

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.067
in the middle of the first kind
of wave of COVID.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:54.601
And so, I think as probably
everybody made movies

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.801
and tried to make the comparison
between that and COVID.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:58.234
But it did kind of make sense.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:01.300
I mean, we were talking about
dinosaurs every day with my son.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.601
But also this --

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:05.100
making something big
that families could go see.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.267
-Yeah.
-Seemed --

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.501
Seemed good at the time.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:12.167
It was like a big movie.
The scale was really massive.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.667
It was dinosaurs.

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.200
No one asked me
to play that before,

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.534
and it seemed interesting.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:20.334
And that everyone in the family
could see it was just --

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:23.234
and that it was kind of the
metaphor of everyone's fighting

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:25.601
this invisible enemy
that they have no precedent for,

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:28.167
made sense.
-It's also by one of the writers

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.601
of "A Quiet Place" too, as well.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.934
So, it's action, but it's also
kind of a thriller as well.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:34.300
On top of being family.
-It is.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.100
But you -- but kids --
kids can see it.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.634
But, yeah, it is,
hopefully, scary.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:40.467
-Yeah. And how --
is it tricky to act

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:43.033
opposite of, what is it,
a tennis ball?

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.767
What are you acting against?
-You do the, like, the whole

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.234
guy in the green jump suit
and the tennis ball.

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:49.901
That's the only one
that's humiliating.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:53.334
Usually when it's like --
We did it all different ways.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:56.133
They even had the people
dressed up in the whole costume,

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.067
which is terrifying, too,
where they, you know,

00:04:58.067 --> 00:04:59.934
put them in a field,
which is actually terrifying.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.300
It doesn't seem
like it would be,

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.100
but it's scary when you
are actually looking at --

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.267
a life-sized dinosaur.
-And people are chasing you

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.400
through --
-Yeah.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.567
-Yeah, anyone chasing me
through a field,

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:09.601
I would be frightened.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:11.400
-[ Indistinct ]
-Like, just a -- a guy.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.701
-Anyone. Yeah, anyone, yeah.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.601
A child. Anyone chasing me,
I'd go, "Stop chasing me!

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:16.901
Stop chasing me!"
I would freak out.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:18.634
-Yeah, yeah.
-If he's dressed as a dinosaur,

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:19.868
I'd be like,
that's not acting for me.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.300
-Yeah, they had two people
dressed as like a --

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.400
the kind of
a life-size dinosaur.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.701
That was terrifying.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:26.167
But when it's a guy, like,
hitting you in the face

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:29.100
with a tennis ball,
it's just humiliating.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.634
-Yeah, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.767
And so -- I'm happy
that you did it though,

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:35.968
because I think we need
more good, big family movies

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.400
that everyone
can sit around and watch,

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.767
and you bring your kids to,
and everyone watches and enjoys.

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:43.367
-Yeah, to me it was like, that's
one of my favorite parts of --

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:47.067
well, films, they're all over
the map as far as what --

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:48.567
who can consume them when,

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:49.934
and what they mean
at different times,

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:51.567
and the scale of them,
and the size of them,

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.067
and -- and who watches them.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:55.567
And for -- to be a part of ones
where everyone in the family

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.601
can go to and --
I mean that's --

00:05:57.601 --> 00:06:00.534
those are some of my favorite
and rare experiences actually.

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.267
-I love it.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:04.067
Here is Adam Driver in "65."

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:05.267
Take a look at this.

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:08.267
[ Alarm blaring ]

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.267
[ Distant screech ]

00:06:11.267 --> 00:06:20.801
♪♪

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:23.567
[ Distant screech ]

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:27.734
♪♪

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:30.968
[ Thunder clash ]

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:33.434
[ Low growling ]

00:06:33.434 --> 00:06:37.868
♪♪

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:39.534
[ Low snarling ]

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:41.701
Yeah! Come on!

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:42.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:45.067
-I run in Jordans.

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:46.667
-Then you run to Queens.
-Yeah, I run to Queens.

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:49.434
-Then you run to Queens.
Adam Driver, "65"...

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:51.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
...is exclusively in theaters

00:06:51.234 --> 00:06:52.234
this Friday.

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:53.801
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:06:53.801 --> 00:06:54.968
Stick around, everybody.

